// Array Methods Demo
// Demonstrates map, filter, and reduce functions in Prism

// Sample data with confidence
temperatures = [68.5, 72.1, 69.8, 75.3, 71.2] ~> 0.95

// Note: Since Prism doesn't have lambda expressions yet,
// we need to use the LLM to create transformation functions
// or pre-define them as named functions

// Example using array methods with LLM-based transformations:
// This would require the LLM to understand the transformation intent

// For testing purposes, you can define functions programmatically
// in the runtime environment (see array-methods.test.ts)

// The syntax for array methods is:
// - map(array, transformFunction)
// - filter(array, predicateFunction) 
// - reduce(array, reducerFunction, initialValue?)

// Future enhancement: Lambda expressions
// temperatures.map(t => (t - 32) * 5/9)  // Convert F to C
// temperatures.filter(t => t > 70)       // Get warm days
// temperatures.reduce((sum, t) => sum + t, 0) / temperatures.length  // Average

